{"abstract":"We present a Research through Design exploration of the potential for using tangible and embodied interactions to enable active music experiences - musicking - for non-musicians. We present the Tubularium prototype, which aims to facilitate music-making to non-musicians by not requiring any initial skill while still eliciting agency and overall, providing a meaningful experience. We present the design of the prototype and the features implemented and reflect on insights from a public event in which the prototype was trialed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818255"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Embodied interaction","Musicking","Non Musicians","Research through Design","Tangible interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enabling embodied music making for non musicians","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15699662","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818255","identifier":[{"id":"105010843977","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f4b27c41-80c3-4a4f-aa9b-41866214f073"],"keyword":["Embodied Interaction","Musicking","Non-Musicians","Research through Design","Tangible Interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3A6964F02285C03B092FBC3AF383CD4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15699662","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucía","key":"montesínospau","last":"Montesínos","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","name_org":"Montesínos, Lucía","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan Hauch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82a68906-d29e-47d3-9b30-ab8c6e916283","name":"Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-6489","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","name_org":"Løvlie, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.15699662","pages":"1-7","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010843977"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f4b27c41-80c3-4a4f-aa9b-41866214f073"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enabling Embodied Music-Making for Non-Musicians","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818255","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"GenFrame is an interactive picture frame that mimics traditional paintings while being equipped with generative AI capabilities. Painting \"portraits of a girl\"has been a trope in art history for centuries. However, in the era of generative AI models, the permanence of traditional art is challenged. When an AI model is able to mimic any painting style, it can also give agency to the viewer to repaint the painting per individual desires. In this installation, we modify the role of the museum placard to provide a minimal tangible interface to change the style of the image and the mood of the depicted girl. In this way, the generative AI model is interfaced in tangible ways, instead of the regular prompt paradigm.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Risi, Sebastian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810858"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["AI art","Generative AI","Image Generation","Interactive art"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genframe an interactive picture frame painting the portrait of any girl","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665437","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810858","identifier":[{"id":"85198907015","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ba56ce57-55c5-4227-9110-1104cf6fc32a"],"keyword":["AI art","AI-generated painting","generative AI","image generation","interactive art"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-72F7A198D25F70B3955D47B1C4B823CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665437","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444851222/GenFrame.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3665437","eisbn":["9798400706325"],"pages":"353-358","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","series":"DIS 2024 - Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","status":"p","title":"DIS 2024 - Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198907015"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ba56ce57-55c5-4227-9110-1104cf6fc32a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GenFrame : An Interactive Picture Frame Painting the Portrait of Any Girl","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-810858","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a Research through Design exploration of the potential for using tangible interactions to enable active music experiences - musicking - for non-musicians. We present the Tubularium prototype, which aims to help non-musicians play music without requiring any initial skill. We present the initial design of the prototype and the features implemented in order to enable music-making by non-musicians, and offer some reflections based on observations of informal initial user explorations of the prototype.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Jensen, Halfdan Hauch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747259"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Music","Musicking","Research through Design","Tangible interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using tangible interaction to design musicking artifacts for non musicians","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2404.09597.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747259","ids":["itu-b7531ccc-7d89-43cd-b9ea-63cdc1b8838c"],"keyword":["Music","Musicking","Research through Design","tangible interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01AACD3125C7F80F7B2536C2ABE3431D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.09597","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2404.09597.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucia","key":"montesinosgarciapau","last":"Montesinos Garcia","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos Garcia, Lucia","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan Hauch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82a68906-d29e-47d3-9b30-ab8c6e916283","name":"Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-6489","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7531ccc-7d89-43cd-b9ea-63cdc1b8838c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Tangible Interaction to Design Musicking Artifacts for Non-musicians","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747259","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This Research through Design paper explores how object detection may be applied to a large digital art museum collection to facilitate new ways of encountering and experiencing art. We present the design and evaluation of an interactive application called SMKExplore, which allows users to explore a museum’s digital collection of paintings by browsing through objects detected in the images, as a novel form of open-ended exploration. We provide three contributions. First, we show how an object detection pipeline can be integrated into a design process for visual exploration. Second, we present the design and development of an app that enables exploration of an art museum’s collection. Third, we offer reflections on future possibilities for museums and HCI researchers to incorporate object detection techniques into the digitalization of museums.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Meyer, Louie Søs","Engel Aaen, Johanne","Tranberg, Anitamalina Regitse","Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Risi, Sebastian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776388"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Art","Computer vision","Experience Design","Exploratory search","Object detection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithmic ways of seeing using object detection to facilitate art exploration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776388","identifier":[{"id":"85194821101","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36e89c8e-4de8-41b5-bd2b-cb15b82c34c9"],"keyword":["Art","Computer Vision","Experience Design","Exploratory Search","Object Detection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-999A595D22DDB832C9D963ECCFE52A4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642157","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louie Søs","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"b55a7155-5e64-4230-b7da-94f7872e9742","name":"Meyer, Louie Søs","orcid":"0009-0008-7490-3049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanne","key":"engelaaenpau","last":"Engel Aaen","name":"Engel Aaen, Johanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anitamalina Regitse","key":"tranbergpau","last":"Tranberg","name":"Tranberg, Anitamalina Regitse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","locid":"f30d35c6-4320-476f-8506-481764e6009e","name":"Kun, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0778-7662","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3613904.3642157","pages":"1-18","series":"ACM Annual Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","status":"p","title":"Algorithmic Ways of Seeing: Using Object Detection to Facilitate Art Exploration"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194821101"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36e89c8e-4de8-41b5-bd2b-cb15b82c34c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Algorithmic Ways of Seeing: Using Object Detection to Facilitate Art Exploration","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776388","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Ongoing efforts to turn Machine Learning (ML) into a design material have encountered limited success. This paper examines the burgeoning area of AI art to understand how artists incorporate ML in their creative work. Drawing upon related HCI theories, we investigate how artists create ambiguity by analyzing nine AI artworks that use computer vision and image synthesis. Our analysis shows that, in addition to the established types of ambiguity, artists worked closely with the ML process (dataset curation, model training, and application) and developed various techniques to evoke the ambiguity of processes. Our finding indicates that the current conceptualization of ML as a design material needs to reframe the ML process as design elements, instead of technical details. Finally, this paper offers reflections on commonly held assumptions in HCI about ML uncertainty, dependability, and explainability, and advocates to supplement the artifact-centered design perspective of ML with a process-centered one.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Salimbeni, Guido","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Benford, Steve","Zhu, Jichen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747257"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Ambiguity","Art","Artificial intelligence","Computer vision","Generative art","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine learning processes as sources of ambiguity insights from ai art","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642855","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747257","identifier":[{"id":"85194816490","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b1c4ca86-1082-449f-aeec-78a7a3b05bba"],"keyword":["ambiguity","art","artificial intelligence","computer vision","generative art","machine learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CEBB89AAD8A5D37E98E491E87878EE76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642855","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guido","key":"salimbenipau","last":"Salimbeni","name":"Salimbeni, Guido","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steve","key":"benfordpau","last":"Benford","name":"Benford, Steve","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3613904.3642855","eisbn":["9798400703300"],"pages":"1-14","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194816490"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b1c4ca86-1082-449f-aeec-78a7a3b05bba"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Machine Learning Processes as Sources of Ambiguity : Insights from AI Art","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747257","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Deep Generative Models (DGM) have had a great impact both on visual art and broader visual culture. In this research-through-design project we investigate the use of a DGM for helping museum visitors explore the aesthetics of Edvard Munch’s art. We designed and built an interactive drawing table that allows a user to explore a StyleGAN model trained on sketches by Edvard Munch. The paper makes two novel contributions: 1. It presents a system that allows users to interact with a DGM by drawing on paper (rather than the typical text prompts used by most current systems). 2. We demonstrate how this mode and quality of interaction establish a unique perspective on Munch’s drawings as a practice. Through qualitative evaluation, we discuss how this setup led users towards a specific hermeneutic drawing strategy that enables building competency with the model and by proxy the data it is trained on. We suggest that the resulting interaction may contribute to an \"education of attention\" helping museum visitors to become attentive to certain visual qualities in Munch’s drawing practice. Finally, we discuss how the concepts of technological mediation and relationality are useful for designing how the output of a DGM is understood by its users.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759390"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Deep generative models","Drawing","Fine Art","Interaction design","Machine learning","Postphenomenology","StyleGAN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring aesthetic qualities of deep generative models through technological art mediation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661498","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759390","identifier":[{"id":"85200339472","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-19834b9c-af5e-46ba-b60e-a95c61f3849a"],"keyword":["Deep generative models","StyleGAN","aesthetics","drawing","fine art","interaction design","machine learning","postphenomenology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-613A6EB589308DFB0A243AF2450537F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661498","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661498","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"isbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"2738-2752","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200339472"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-19834b9c-af5e-46ba-b60e-a95c61f3849a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring Aesthetic Qualities of Deep Generative Models through Technological (Art) Mediation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759390","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Image-generation AI models have triggered a paradigm shift in how we can express ourselves in visual art. Despite their widespread use in a short amount of time, embedding these models into interactive artifacts is still largely unexplored. In this pictorial, we unpack the design and development process of GenFrame, an image generating picture frame that utilizes generative AI capabilities to mimic traditional paintings. Our work details the necessary steps to integrate generative AI into interactive artifacts and highlights important design considerations for controlling image-generation models in order to achieve specific design intents. Our insights provide interaction designers with a more comprehensive understanding and approach towards utilizing image-generation AI models for interactive artifacts. A demo can be viewed at https://youtu.be/1rhW4fazaBY.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809172"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cultural heritage","Interaction design","Museums"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genframe embedding generative ai into interactive artifacts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809172","identifier":[{"id":"85198907112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"keyword":["cultural heritage","image-generation AI models","interaction design","museums"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6705AE38DF230903B57FF9F32135C96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444850486/GenFrame_Embedding_Generative_AI_Into_Interactive_Artifacts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias Anton","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","name_org":"Freiberger, Matthias Anton","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3660750","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"714-727","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198907112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GenFrame – Embedding Generative AI Into Interactive Artifacts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809172","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Models leveraging both visual and textual data such as Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training (CLIP), are the backbone of many recent advances in artificial intelligence. In this work, we show that despite their versatility, such models are vulnerable to what we refer to as fooling master images. Fooling master images are capable of maximizing the confidence score of a CLIP model for a significant number of widely varying prompts, while being either unrecognizable or unrelated to the attacked prompts for humans. We demonstrate how fooling master images can be mined using stochastic gradient descent, projected gradient descent, or gradient-free optimisation. Contrary to many common adversarial attacks, the gradient-free optimisation approach allows us to mine fooling examples even when the weights of the model are not accessible. We investigate the properties of the mined fooling master images, and find that images trained on a small number of image captions potentially generalize to a much larger number of semantically related captions. Finally, we evaluate possible mitigation strategies and find that vulnerability to fooling master examples appears to be closely related to a modality gap in contrastive pre-trained multi-modal networks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Freiberger, Matthias","Kun, Peter","Igel, Christian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799221"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fooling contrastive language image pre trained models with clipmasterprints","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/445732914/Fooling_Contrastive.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799221","identifier":[{"id":"85219537520","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-32b0a564-5425-44f1-8c65-0e2a4d0f4230"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-53D3BE5C256BFF74DA1453D5EE87C02D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/445732914/Fooling_Contrastive.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=ZFZnvGXXMm","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"igelpau","last":"Igel","locid":"4ecc5e2e-7589-4f9b-9f79-d5dd99f56311","name":"Igel, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2868-0856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["28358856"],"issue":"4","journal":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","volume":"2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219537520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-32b0a564-5425-44f1-8c65-0e2a4d0f4230"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fooling Contrastive Language-Image Pre-Trained Models with CLIPMasterPrints.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799221","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT This article accounts for the process of co-constructing knowledge as a set of recommendations on digital and organizational change for the museum sector. The recommendations were formulated at the end of an 18-month-long action research project with 10 participating museums from EU and the USA. Here we analyze the contextual background for the recommendations and show how the initially open knowledge generating process was stepwise condensed into four so-called How Might We questions that served as the foundation for outlining the final recommendations. The article provides an overview of a design thinking process that could be applied in other museums and thereby contributes with an informative account of how design-led processes can be employed to support museums in facilitating organizational change.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mortensen, Christian Hviid","Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Malde, Sejul"],"cuid":["S02-092.64-751866"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Mortensen, Christian Hviid"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University"],"keyword":["Action research","Design","Digital technologies","Innovation","Organizational change","co constructed knowledge"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kvorning Design"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how might we co constructing recommendations on digital and organizational change","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/209335483/MMC_manus_submit_final_rev_clean_PURE_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["In this article, we will provide a detailed account of how design-led processes can be employed to support museums in adapting to the current digital transformation and related organizational changes. These processes revolved around the co-construction of knowledge and resulted in a set of recommendations for the museum sector. The recommendations are published as part of The GIFT Box–a website containing various open access resources for museums developed within the GIFT Project funded by the EU’s Horizon 2020 initiative (GIFT ). Therefore, this article acts as a companion piece to the recommendations on the website by providing a deep dive into the design-led processes and background materials underpinning the actual recommendations. Here we will show how the recommendations were developed in a collaborative and iterative process between researchers and museum professionals. In order to disassemble siloed ways of thinking (Tett ) and explore new opportunities, we engaged ten museum professionals in an 18-month cross-institutional and cross-national action research process – a method to engage directly with the challenges we face through reflection, experimentation and evaluation (Mortensen et al. )."],"id":"S02-092.64-751866","identifier":[{"id":"85136155277","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8e79019f-cf37-4125-bdb7-3858cc4ef0f5","sdu-4a90cf0d-1415-4cf1-ba83-6ab1749fdcd2"],"keyword":["action research","co-constructed knowledge","design","digital technologies","innovation","organizational change"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-09CE83AF2BAA15A157FAF01CEA1316B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/209335483/MMC_manus_submit_final_rev_clean_PURE_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93087783/MMC_manus_submit_final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture, Media Science","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Kvorning Design"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"australian national university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Australian National University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Hviid","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"3cdf6e8d-ed45-4136-84fd-408f346ba53c","name":"Mortensen, Christian Hviid","orcid":"0000-0001-9822-1714","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Rørbæk","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sejul","key":"maldepau","last":"Malde","name":"Malde, Sejul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09647775.2022.2111332","issn":["09647775","18729185"],"issn_org":["09647775"],"issue":"4","journal":"Museum Management and Curatorship","pages":"419-432","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Museum Management and Curatorship","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136155277"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e79019f-cf37-4125-bdb7-3858cc4ef0f5","sdu-4a90cf0d-1415-4cf1-ba83-6ab1749fdcd2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How might we? Co-constructing recommendations on digital and organizational change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.64-751866","year":2024,"yearsub":2024}
{"abstract":"New Snow is an interactive drawing table that investigates human interaction with a deep generative model based on Edvard Munch’s sketching practice. Through drawings with pen and paper, the user can interact with the model which will return synthetic sketches based on the input drawings in real time. The model is a reflection of the training data, and it is thus constrained to representing images within the latent space of Edvard Munch’s sketching practice. As the user familiarizes themselves with the model it allows them to become sensitized to the visual aesthetic belonging to this practice. This potential for familiarization with the aesthetic of a dataset via the model has implications for human-AI interaction and non-verbal art mediation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Haas, René","Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677299"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Edvard Munch","Generative model","Human AI interaction","Interactive Drawing Table","Visual Aesthetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring a digital art collection through drawing interactions with a deep generative model","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544549.3583902","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677299","identifier":[{"id":"85158103861","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-192a7e77-f4ba-4bce-a7f4-3f89c222d9de"],"keyword":["Edvard Munch","Generative Model","Human-AI Interaction","Interactive Drawing Table","Visual Aesthetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-452AAEA103BB0F57C7BFD6BD8AAFFE4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544549.3583902","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/97264390/New_Snow_CHI_Interactivity_2023_submitted_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3544549.3583902","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan Hauch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"82a68906-d29e-47d3-9b30-ab8c6e916283","name":"Jensen, Halfdan Hauch","orcid":"0000-0002-0351-6489","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544549.3583902","eisbn":["9781450394222/23/04"],"pages":"1-5","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Extended Abstracts of the 2023 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","title":"CHI EA '23"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85158103861"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-192a7e77-f4ba-4bce-a7f4-3f89c222d9de"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring a Digital Art Collection through Drawing Interactions with a Deep Generative Model","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677299","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Thea Overby","Jensen, Maria Leis","Tonnesen, Line Schack","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718825"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stairway to heaven designing for an embodied experience with satellite data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102813090/Stairway_to_Heaven_Designing_for_an_Embodied_Experience_with_Sat.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718825","ids":["itu-08de88d4-b65d-4c84-9f2a-8916240747fd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F79160BF18F71B351948B37939AC6684"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/iasdr/iasdr2023/shortpapers/1/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102813090/Stairway_to_Heaven_Designing_for_an_Embodied_Experience_with_Sat.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea Overby","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thea Overby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Leis","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Maria Leis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Schack","key":"tonnesenpau","last":"Tonnesen","name":"Tonnesen, Line Schack","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"IASDR 2023: Life Changing Design"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-08de88d4-b65d-4c84-9f2a-8916240747fd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stairway to Heaven: Designing for an Embodied Experience with Satellite Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718825","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Widespread concerns about the spread of misinformation have gained urgency during the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic and pose challenges for science journalism, in particular in the health area. This article reports on a Research through Design study exploring how to design a tool for helping readers of science journalism understand the strength and uncertainty of scientific evidence in news stories about health science, using both textual and visual information. A central aim has been to teach readers about criteria for assessing scientific evidence, in particular in order to help readers differentiate between science and pseudoscience. Working in a research-in-the-wild collaboration with a website for popular science, the study presents the design and evaluation of the Scientific Evidence Indicator, which uses metadata about scientific publications to present an assessment of evidence strength to the readers. Evaluations of the design demonstrate some success in helping readers recognize whether studies have undergone scientific peer review or not, but also point to challenges in facilitating a more in-depth understanding. Insights from the study point to a potential for developing similar tools aimed at journalists rather than directly at audiences.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Waagstein, Astrid","Hyldgård, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718877"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Design","Evidence","Health","Human Computer Interaction","Misinformation","Science journalism","Uncertainty"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Sciencecom Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how trustworthy is this research designing a tool to help readers understand evidence and uncertainty in science journalism","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102813079/2202.00069.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718877","identifier":[{"id":"85151497341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8534e2cd-0329-4363-90e1-39f0d7f41339"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Science journalism","design","evidence","health","human-computer interaction","misinformation","uncertainty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-689285AA7E11DE3886B5920ACE64C7DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.00069","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102813079/2202.00069.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Sciencecom Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"waagsteinpau","last":"Waagstein","name":"Waagstein, Astrid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"hyldgårdpau","last":"Hyldgård","name":"Hyldgård, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21670811","2167082X"],"issn_org":["21670811"],"issue":"3","journal":"Digital Journalism","pages":"431-464","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Digital Journalism","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151497341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8534e2cd-0329-4363-90e1-39f0d7f41339"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“How Trustworthy Is This Research?” Designing a Tool to Help Readers Understand Evidence and Uncertainty in Science Journalism","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718877","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present and discuss a user-study prototype, developed for the Bakkehuset historic house museum in Copenhagen. We examine how the prototype—a digital sound installation—can expand visitors’ experiences of the house and offer encounters with immaterial cultural heritage. Historic house museums often hold back on utilizing digital communication tools inside the houses, since a central purpose of this type of museum is to preserve an original environment. Digital communication tools, however, hold great potential for facilitating rich encounters with cultural heritage and in particular with the immaterial aspects of museum collections and their histories. In this article, we present our design steps and choices, aiming at subtly and seamlessly adding a digital dimension to a historic house. Based on qualitative interviews, we evaluate how the sound installation at Bakkehuset is sensed, interpreted, and used by visitors as part of their museum experience. In turn, we shed light on the historic house museum as a distinct design context for designing hybrid visitor experiences and point to the potentials of digital communication tools in this context.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Falch Yates, Mia","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718912"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Heritage","historic house museums","hybrid designs","immaterial cultural","museum experience design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subtle sound design designing for experience blend in a historic house museum","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102488217/Subtle_Sound_Design_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718912","identifier":[{"id":"85188349520","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c0851b38-def9-4ac3-be59-b589ac400bd1"],"keyword":["heritage","historic house museums","hybrid designs","immaterial cultural","museum experience design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25854E844FFE852FE208697096649755"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102488217/Subtle_Sound_Design_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia","key":"falchyatespau","last":"Falch Yates","name":"Falch Yates, Mia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3633476","issn":["15564673","15564711"],"issn_org":["15564673"],"journal":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188349520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c0851b38-def9-4ac3-be59-b589ac400bd1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Subtle Sound Design: Designing for Experience Blend in a Historic House Museum","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718912","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Foka, Anna","Eklund, Lina","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Griffin, Gabriele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718930"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"critically assessing ai ml for cultural heritage potentials and challenges","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181784910","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718930","identifier":[{"id":"85181784910","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e88ef222-ace3-4f17-840f-b22940074fac"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-B99458A222D87C0572DA0824B5A2E03D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"fokapau","last":"Foka","name":"Foka, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Lina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriele","key":"griffinpau","last":"Griffin","name":"Griffin, Gabriele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Simon","key":"lindgrenpedh","last":"Lindgren","name":"Lindgren, Simon","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781803928562.00082","eisbn":["9781803928562"],"isbn":["9781803928555"],"pages":"815-825","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"Handbook of Critical Studies of Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181784910"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e88ef222-ace3-4f17-840f-b22940074fac"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Critically assessing AI/ML for cultural heritage: potentials and challenges","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718930","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The use of technology in art museums is usually limited to communicating verbal information such as interpretive text and audio guides, or to facilitating social experiences. This paper presents a Research through Design study of an immersive room-scale installation in an art museum. The aim was to afford non-verbal art mediation and educate the attention of museum visitors to certain aspects of a series of paintings. The installation was based on recent art historical research and aimed to use this research to facilitate a new perspective on the artworks. The installation was created through a one-year-long iterative process that involved diverse stakeholder groups of experts, visitors, and non-visitors in testing and formative evaluation. The final design was part of the opening of the new [XX] museum in October 2021 and was visited by almost 80,000 people in four months. Through interviews with 47 visitors, we evaluate how their experience corresponds with the design intent, and how the installation through non-verbal means drew their attention to aspects of the related artwork. We find that the installation largely evokes the intended aesthetic qualities and support reflection on Edvard Munch’s life and artistic practice. Finally, we discuss the use of education of attention as a lens for design practitioners to conceptualize and evaluate how their designs mediate learning and interpretive practices for art museum visitors.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Mathias, Nikita","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718849"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","South Africa"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","MUNCH","University of the Free State"],"keyword":["Art Mediation","Design","Education of Attention","Immersive"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"educating the attention of museum visitors through non verbal art mediation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/iasdr.2023.222","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718849","ids":["itu-45ec16e4-d697-407b-9f94-1aae53f87b27"],"keyword":["Art Mediation","Design","Education of Attention","Immersive"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9676E1BBDDF9C002CBFFE9BEE6B98D8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/iasdr.2023.222","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1075&context=iasdr","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"munch","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"MUNCH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"za","key":"university of the free state","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of the Free State","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3",