{"abstract":"Abstract Introduces the concept of hybrid museum experiences, why it is timely, and presents the major theme of the book: How to make museum experiences more personally and socially meaningful through the use of technology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Waern, Annika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384702"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Digital cultural heritage","Hybrid museum experiences","Museum technology integration","Personal and social meaning","Visitor Engagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100079/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384702","ids":["itu-e8e1a42c-6d8b-4805-8848-dd4173cb0147"],"keyword":["Digital cultural heritage","Hybrid museum experiences","Museum technology integration","Personal and social meaning","Visitor engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BB9CF9E199CCB00F0C1ABE6473A0EB0D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100079/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"waernpau","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annika","key":"waernpedh","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepedh","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789048552849"],"publisher":"Amsterdam University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Theory and Design","title":"Hybrid Museum Experiences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8e1a42c-6d8b-4805-8848-dd4173cb0147"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384702","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT Museums have increasingly focused on digital technologies and play as means to provide personalized, engaging experiences for their audience. Balancing educational and playful values is often conflicting. To address that conflict, museums often employ participatory design strategies. However, those strategies usually end after the deployment of those experiences, thus they do not accommodate for what occurs during actual use. In this article, we follow Light House, a research-through-design experiment of an installation that was developed using an iterative design approach which expands on actual use by deploying undetermined artefacts to support the discovery of novel interactions by visitors. Through our findings, we explore the “failure” of Light House to support the discovery of such interactions in relation to its educational character, but rather it inspired people to incorporate it in the activities supported by the surrounding space. Finally, we discuss the implications those discovered interactions in terms of potential re-design directions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ioannidis, Petros","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384967"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital technologies","Interactive Installations","Iterative design","Museum Engagement","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring affordances through design after design the re purposing of an exhibition artefact by museum visitors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93084742/Creativity_and_Cognition_2022.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384967","identifier":[{"id":"85133334855","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fb45146c-311d-4f33-bfad-f5cd167b9c51"],"keyword":["Digital Technologies","Interactive Installations","Iterative Design","Museum Engagement","Participatory Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0ED69939892311741577371E5720BF4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93084742/Creativity_and_Cognition_2022.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petros","key":"ioannidispau","last":"Ioannidis","name":"Ioannidis, Petros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3527927.3532802","pages":"125-134","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"C&amp;C '22: Creativity and Cognition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133334855"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fb45146c-311d-4f33-bfad-f5cd167b9c51"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring affordances through design-after-design: the re-purposing of an exhibition artefact by museum visitors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384967","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
