{"abstract":"Abstract The final chapter of the book draws some perspective back to the first chapters, focussing on how hybrid museum experiences may also challenge museums in unforeseen ways. We charter the ways in which a hybrid museum experience can change the way a museum is experienced. Depending on context and the reasons for introducing a hybrid experience, these changes can be seen as design opportunities, but they may also challenge the expectations of stakeholders, including both museum professionals and visitors. In order to make informed design choices in a design project, it is important to be critically aware of these expectations","author_count":4,"contributors":["Waern, Annika","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383558"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Design Opportunities","Hybrid Museum Experience","Museum Innovation","Stakeholder Expectations","Visitor Engagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"remediating reframing and restaging the museum","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100885/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383558","ids":["itu-9cd50ae6-e328-4564-819d-02446cbf586e"],"keyword":["Design Opportunities","Hybrid Museum Experience","Museum Innovation","Stakeholder Expectations","Visitor Engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E15D6CA947A2CFE3354B04BC3E7A38D5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100885/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"waernpau","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annika","key":"waernpedh","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepedh","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789048552849"],"pages":"197-211","publisher":"Amsterdam University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Theory and Design","title":"Hybrid Museum Experiences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9cd50ae6-e328-4564-819d-02446cbf586e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Remediating, Reframing and Restaging the Museum","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383558","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Abstract This chapter argues for the importance of ideation in design processes. We present three paper-based tools for ideation to be used at a meeting or a workshop tailored specifically to the museum sector and developed in collaboration with museum professionals. Each tool targets a different phase of the design process. There is a tool for generating ideas, strengthening ideas and testing ideas. The chapter accounts for the what, when, how and why of these ideation tools. Finally, we discuss how the tools can be used in combination and how they can encourage reflection.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","Mortensen, Christian Hviid","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S02-090.62-038396"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design processes","Ideation","Museum Sector","Paper based Tools","Professional Collaboration"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kvorning Design"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ideation tools for experience design","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100695/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.62-038396","ids":["itu-ded3ba60-52d9-42ae-961f-8737c609d9e0","sdu-62b046bd-21c3-4c7c-a3c1-9d2d08ceddbe"],"keyword":["Design Processes","Ideation","Museum Sector","Paper-based Tools","Professional Collaboration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-F85117CE0BFDE5CC8E4D06EB516AEC52"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/9789048552849-009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93100695/Hybrid_Museum_Experiences.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Kvorning Design"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science, Media Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Rørbæk","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Hviid","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"3cdf6e8d-ed45-4136-84fd-408f346ba53c","name":"Mortensen, Christian Hviid","orcid":"0000-0001-9822-1714","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annika","key":"waernpedh","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"løvliepedh","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","eisbn":["9789048552849"],"isbn":["9789463726443"],"pages":"145-156","place":"Amsterdam","publisher":"Amsterdam University Press","series":"MediaMatters","status":"p","subtitle":"Theory and Design","title":"Hybrid Museum Experiences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ded3ba60-52d9-42ae-961f-8737c609d9e0","sdu-62b046bd-21c3-4c7c-a3c1-9d2d08ceddbe"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Ideation Tools for Experience Design","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.62-038396","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a research through design exploration using tangible interactions in order to seamlessly integrate technology in a historical house museum. The study addresses a longstanding concern in museum exhibition design that interactive technologies may distract from the artifacts on display. Through an iterative design process including user studies, a co-creation workshop with museum staff and several prototypes, we developed an interactive installation called \\textit{The Diary of Niels} that combines physical objects, RFID sensors and an elaborate fiction in order to facilitate increased visitor engagement. Insights from the research process and user tests indicate that the integration of technology and artifacts is meaningful and engaging for users, and helps introduce museum visitors to the historic theme of the exhibition and the meaning of the artifacts. The study also points to continued challenges in integrating such hybrid experiences fully with the rest of the exhibition.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schou, Mette Muxoll","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382024"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Historical house museum","Interactive technologies","Museum exhibition design","Tangible interactions","User engagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the diary of niels affective engagement through tangible interaction with museum artifacts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85513401/The_Diary_of_Niels_camera_ready.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382024","identifier":[{"id":"85105944945","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-33978b8a-4750-4b06-afd4-f89964b7a920"],"keyword":["Historical house museum","Interactive technologies","Museum exhibition design","Tangible interactions","User engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E80DD71EF38621F0BAB89EB3C3DFA2E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85513401/The_Diary_of_Niels_camera_ready.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Muxoll","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Mette Muxoll","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-73043-7_24","eisbn":["9783030730437"],"isbn":["9783030730420"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"289-299","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Digital Heritage. Progress in Cultural Heritage: Documentation, Preservation, and Protection","title":"EuroMed 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105944945"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-33978b8a-4750-4b06-afd4-f89964b7a920"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Diary of Niels: Affective engagement through tangible interaction with museum artifacts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382024","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"he senses are finding their way back into the art museum, but the way paintings are displayed is still constrained by their fragility. We explore whether it would be helpful to use the capabilities of digital technologies to create meaningful somaesthetic experiences with digital reproductions. We conducted an experiment with 19 participants, letting them handle physical paintings and 2D and 3D digital reproductions, while ranking them according to their personal preference. To discover which cultural qualities participants ascribe to artworks in light of their somaesthetic experience, we interviewed participants regarding their experience of ranking three setups. We found that participants regarded the 3D reproductions as having certain material qualities. We argue that by designing the somaesthetic experience of digital reproductions, it might be possible to bring back dimensions of the art experience that were lost with the development of the modern museum.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384791"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Art experience","Post Phenomenology","Somaesthetics","digital reproductions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling digital reproductions of artworks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://somaesthetics.aau.dk/index.php/JOS/article/view/6688/6032","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384791","identifier":[{"id":"85124980598","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ef64fd73-16dc-4dc1-a3ed-b7c2089bf503"],"keyword":["art experience","digital reproductions","post-phenomenology","somaesthetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D3BAC214473058C6D449111299CA7D9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://somaesthetics.aau.dk/index.php/JOS/article/view/6688/6032","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22468498"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Somaesthetics","pages":"51-71","publisher":"Aalborg Universitet","status":"p","title":"Journal of Somaesthetics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ef64fd73-16dc-4dc1-a3ed-b7c2089bf503"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Handling digital reproductions of artworks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384791","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present a lifecycle study of We Dare You, a substitutional reality installation that combines visual and tactile stimuli. The installation is set up in a center for architecture, and invites visitors to explore its facade while playing with vertigo, in a visual virtual reality environment that replicates the surrounding physical space of the installation. Drawing on an ethnographic approach, including observations and interviews, we researched the exhibit from its opening, through the initial months plagued by technical problems, its subsequent success as a social and playful installation, on to its closure, due to COVID-19, and its subsequent reopening. Our findings explore the challenges caused by both the hybrid nature of the installation and the visitors’ playful use of the installation which made the experience social and performative—but also caused some problems. We also discuss the problems We Dare You faced in light of hygiene demands due to COVID-19. The analysis contrasts the design processes and expectations of stakeholders with the audience’s playful appropriation, which led the stakeholders to see the installation as both a success and a failure. Evaluating the design and redesign through use on behalf of visitors, we argue that an approach that further opens up the post-production experience to a process of continuous redesign based on the user input—what has been termed design-after-design—could facilitate the design of similar experiences in the museum and heritage sector, supporting a participatory agenda in the design process, and helping to resolve the tension between stakeholders’ expectations and visitors’ playful appropriations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ioannidis, Petros","Eklund, Lina","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382260"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Appropriation","Design after design","Mixed reality","Museum","Play","sensory museology","substitutional reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we dare you a lifecycle study of a substitutional reality installation in a museum space","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86249063/2012.01792.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382260","identifier":[{"id":"85111762102","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42d98f82-ded0-44be-9dae-6ccade90857c"],"keyword":["appropriation","design-after-design","mixed reality","museum","play","sensory museology","substitutional reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37EFB8CAADE8A5638E5BA01D51655A95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86249063/2012.01792.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petros","key":"ioannidispau","last":"Ioannidis","name":"Ioannidis, Petros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Lina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3439862","issn":["15564673","15564711"],"issn_org":["15564673"],"issue":"3","journal":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage","pages":"1-21","paperid":"34","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111762102"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42d98f82-ded0-44be-9dae-6ccade90857c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"We Dare You: A Lifecycle Study of a Substitutional Reality Installation in a Museum Space","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382260","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Kadish, David","Risi, Sebastian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381433"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving object detection in art images using only style transfer","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.06529","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381433","ids":["itu-0bc7e113-9fb8-4316-b763-ec7529e03c2d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9EB235CE31B9C34E38D84FBA2AF8DEEE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.06529","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"kadishpau","last":"Kadish","name":"Kadish, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21614407"],"journal":"2021 International Joint Conference on Neural Networks","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2021 International Joint Conference on Neural Networks","title_org":"2021 International Joint Conference on Neural Networks (IJCNN)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0bc7e113-9fb8-4316-b763-ec7529e03c2d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improving Object Detection in Art Images Using Only Style Transfer","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381433","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We reflect on two museum visiting experiences that adopted the strategy of interpersonalization in which one visitor creates an experience for another. In the Gift app, visitors create personal mini-tours for specific others. In Never let me go, one visitor controls the experience of another by sending them remote instructions as they follow them around the museum. By reflecting on the design of these experiences and their deployment in museums we show how interpersonalization can deliver engaging social visits in which visitors make their own interpretations. We contrast the approach to previous research in customization and algorithmic personalization. We reveal how these experiences relied on intimacy between pairs of visitors but also between visitors and the museum. We propose that interpersonalization requires museums to step back to make space for interpretation, but that this then raises the challenge of how to reintroduce the museum's own perspective. Finally, we articulate strategies and challenges for applying this approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ryding, Karin","Spence, Jocelyn","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","BENFORD, STEVE"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-385002"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Experience Design","Gifting","Intimacy","Museum Experiences","Personalization","interpersonalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interpersonalizing intimate museum experiences","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2011.11386","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-385002","identifier":[{"id":"85100250338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-feaff500-1468-4b6f-abed-14ee7d6d067c"],"keyword":["experience design","gifting","interpersonalization","intimacy","museum experiences","personalization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-BDA747C06391469C5B985096262ACD4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2011.11386","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.11386","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"rydingpau","last":"Ryding","name":"Ryding, Karin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jocelyn","key":"spencepau","last":"Spence","name":"Spence, Jocelyn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"STEVE","key":"benfordpau","last":"BENFORD","name":"BENFORD, STEVE","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2011.11386","issn":["10447318","15327590"],"issn_org":["10447318"],"issue":"12","journal":"International Journal of Human-Computer Interaction","pages":"1151-1172","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100250338"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-feaff500-1468-4b6f-abed-14ee7d6d067c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interpersonalizing Intimate Museum Experiences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-385002","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This article brings together two distinct, but related perspectives on playful museum experiences: Critical play and hybrid design. The article explores the challenges involved in combining these two perspectives, through the design of two hybrid museum experiences that aimed to facilitate critical play with/in the collections of the Museum of Yugoslavia and the highly contested heritage they represent. Based on reflections from the design process as well as feedback from test users, we describe a series of challenges: Challenging the norms of visitor behaviour, challenging the role of the artefact, and challenging the curatorial authority. In conclusion, we outline some possible design strategies to address these challenges.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Ryding, Karin","Spence, Jocelyn","Rajkoska, Paulina","Waern, Annika","Wray, Tim","Benford, Steve","William, Preston","Clare-Thorn, Emily"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382870"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Contested heritage","Critical Play","Experience Design","Hybrid Experiences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"playing games with tito designing hybrid museum experiences for critical play","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86489969/2101.12533.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382870","identifier":[{"id":"85108026232","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6bb7bf8e-2f97-47ae-9989-580cf6efb9c1"],"keyword":["Contested heritage","Critical play","Experience design","Hybrid experiences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D97BB4A7A5AEC66EB3FB6D6904511A75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86489969/2101.12533.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"rydingpau","last":"Ryding","name":"Ryding, Karin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jocelyn","key":"spencepau","last":"Spence","name":"Spence, Jocelyn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paulina","key":"rajkoskapau","last":"Rajkoska","name":"Rajkoska, Paulina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"waernpau","last":"Waern","name":"Waern, Annika","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"wraypau","last":"Wray","name":"Wray, Tim","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steve","key":"benfordpau","last":"Benford","name":"Benford, Steve","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Preston","key":"williampau","last":"William","name":"William, Preston","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily","key":"clarethornpau","last":"Clare-Thorn","name":"Clare-Thorn, Emily","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15564673","15564711"],"issn_org":["15564673"],"issue":"2","journal":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage","pages":"1-26","paperid":"16","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108026232"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6bb7bf8e-2f97-47ae-9989-580cf6efb9c1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Playing Games with Tito : Designing Hybrid Museum Experiences for Critical Play","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382870","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"What does the age of participation look like from the perspective of a museum visitor? Arguably, the concept of participative experiences is already so deeply ingrained in our culture that we may not even think about it as participation. Museum visitors engage in a number of activities, of which observing the exhibits is only one part. Since most visitors come to the museum together with someone else, they spend time and attention on the people they came with, and often the needs of the group are given priority over individual preferences. How can museums tap into these activities - and make themselves relevant to visitors? In this chapter we will try to approach this constructively, as a design opportunity. Could it be productive for the museum to consider itself not only as a disseminator of knowledge, but also as the facilitator of participative activities between visitors? In what follows, we will outline a range of practical design projects that serve as examples of this approach. These projects were part of the European Union funded Horizon2020 project GIFT, a cross-disciplinary collaboration between researchers, artists, designers and many international museums and heritage organisations, exploring the concept of interpersonal museum experiences (see https://gifting.digital/). What the projects have in common is that they build on visitors co-creating and sharing their own narratives in the museum context. We suggest that these projects demonstrate a spectrum of possibilities: From experiences that take place almost without any museum involvement, to those that give museums a role in curating these narratives.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Eklund, Lina","Waern, Annika","Ryding, Karin","Rajkowska, Paulina","Black, Graham"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384168"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nottingham Trent University","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Design Opportunities","Visitor Engagement","co creation narratives","interpersonal museum experiences","participative experiences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for interpersonal museum experiences","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.11398","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384168","ids":["itu-c5d69e60-bacf-4714-b0b0-6858de83a9af"],"keyword":["co-creation narratives","design opportunities","interpersonal museum experiences","participative experiences","visitor engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-490424BF895AD0CF63FE8EFF4CD9217E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.11398","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"nottingham trent university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nottingham Trent University","used":1}],"person":[{"