{"abstract":"Watching television together in the living room is a joyful and social activity that most people can relate to. As a result of the ongoing COVID19 outbreak, many friends and family members are separated due to national lockdowns and quarantine. In this demo we show how a web application can support real-time socially based video-content by facilitating a virtual living room for friends and family where they can watch synchronized video content while interacting. Our prototype uses readily available web-technologies, allowing users to get started in just one click by logging in with their existing YouTube account. Data from the YouTube API are then fed into novel recommender algorithms that then suggest videos based on the user’s collective interests. Info available at https://beta.letswatch.net","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bryld, Jannik Munk","Schønrock, Lucas","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383472"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Recommender algorithms","Synchronized video content","Virtual living room","Web based social interaction","YouTube API"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"watching together but apart shared video experiences during covid 000000000019 outbreak","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383472","ids":["itu-964c92a3-58c7-4aee-adcb-268ef3ebe8c1"],"keyword":["Recommender algorithms","Synchronized video content","Virtual living room","Web-based social interaction","YouTube API"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-938F10934A026D85369215F5369FB323"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://figshare.com/articles/conference_contribution/Demo7_-_Bryld_Sch_nrock_L_vlie_Barkhuus/12496727","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85386004/Bryld_Sch_nrock_L_vlie_Barkhuus_IMX.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik Munk","key":"bryldpau","last":"Bryld","name":"Bryld, Jannik Munk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucas","key":"schønrockpau","last":"Schønrock","name":"Schønrock, Lucas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Adjunct Proceedings of the ACM International Conference on Interactive Media Experiences (IMX) 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-964c92a3-58c7-4aee-adcb-268ef3ebe8c1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Watching Together but Apart: Shared Video Experiences During COVID-19 Outbreak","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383472","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This article presents and discusses a paper-based co-design tool that was developed in order to strengthen ideation in digital experience design processes at museums. The tool, called the ASAP Map, was co-designed as part of an action research project with 10 museums from EU and the USA. The museum partners used the tool in their home institutions and the article focuses on their feedback and the following iterations of the tool through ongoing feedback loops. Concludingly, the usefulness and applicability of the tool is discussed, also touching on the relevance of this study for the broader co-design field.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","Holdgaard, Nanna","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384148"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co design","Collaboration","Design processes","Design tools","Designers","Digital technology","Ideation","Ideation tools","Museums","digital experience design","purpose driven design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co designing a co design tool to strengthen ideation in digital experience design at museums","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85340752/co_designing_a_co_design_tool_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384148","identifier":[{"id":"85089896970","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c4a4566a-36d7-4c1b-8d49-816ad2c2da7f"],"keyword":["co-design","collaboration","design processes","design tools","designers","digital experience design","digital technology","ideation","ideation tools","museums","purpose-driven design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B486D426E0C78BB25ACC64C82096CBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85340752/co_designing_a_co_design_tool_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Rørbæk","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Anne Rørbæk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"holdgaardpau","last":"Holdgaard","name":"Holdgaard, Nanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/15710882.2020.1812668","issn":["15710882","17453755"],"issn_org":["15710882"],"journal":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089896970"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c4a4566a-36d7-4c1b-8d49-816ad2c2da7f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-designing a co-design tool to strengthen ideation in digital experience design at museums","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/sea