u","last":"Ojala","name":"Ojala, Mace","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"The European Commission","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e7b40e49-0406-4afd-acb1-356595b5893c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GIFT Project Deliverable D1.2 Data Management Plan","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384679","year":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This article brings together two separate strands of media research: Online comments and media design. Online comments have long been a topic of much concern, both among scholars and the public at large, fearing negative effects from phenomena such as echo chambers, filter bubbles and hate speech. This paper reports on a project by the Danish public service broadcaster Danmarks Radio, aiming to develop a system for online comments in line with the broadcaster's public service ideals. Through interviews and observations, I explore the challenges encountered by the project team as an empirical case study of cross-disciplinary design work intersecting the fields of design, journalism and new media. I discuss the challenges encountered by the project team in light of Domingo's model of audience participation, suggesting that the broadcaster's strategy represents a development from the \"playgrounds\" model to a \"salon\" model. Building on Löwgren and Reimer's work on collaborative media, I suggest some of the broadcaster's struggles point to a lack of adequate methods for balancing interaction design concerns with the concerns of mass communication and journalism.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383924"],"event":{"acronym":"Mindtrek","title":"Mindtrek conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Audience Participation","Cross disciplinary design","Media design","Online comments","Public service broadcasting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from playground to salon challenges in designing a system for online public debate","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82370423/DR_mindtrek_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383924","identifier":[{"id":"85043254662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b6273a02-9095-44b0-a698-6577d8eb76ca"],"keyword":["Audience participation","Cross-disciplinary design","Media design","Online comments","Public service broadcasting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB60C6C145FAD3614434DF4CB332C118"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82370423/DR_mindtrek_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3131085.3131111","eisbn":["9781450354264"],"pages":"164-173","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"AcademicMindtrek '17 Proceedings of the 21st International Academic Mindtrek Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043254662"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b6273a02-9095-44b0-a698-6577d8eb76ca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Playground to Salon: Challenges in Designing a System for Online Public Debate","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383924","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates user experiences with editorial control in online newspaper comment fields following the public backlash against online comments after the 2011 terror attacks in Norway. We analyze data from a survey of online news consumers focusing on experiences and attitudes towards editorial control set against a spectrum between “interventionist” and “noninterventionist” positions. Results indicate that interventionist respondents rate the quality of online comments as poor, whereas noninterventionist respondents have most often experienced being the target of editorial control measures and feel that editorial control has intensified after the terror attacks. We conclude that newspapers should pay attention to the different needs of participants when devising strategies for editorial control. Media professionals should also consider changes to increase the transparency of moderation practices.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Ihlebæk, Karoline Andrea","Larsson, Anders Olof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382298"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Westerdals Oslo School of Arts"],"keyword":["Editorial Control","Journalism","Moderation","Online comments","User experience","comment fields","communication design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user experiences with editorial control in online newspaper comment fields","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17512786.2017.1293490","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382298","identifier":[{"id":"85014575944","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4573861e-0bb4-49d7-9ebf-defa5924e6b1"],"keyword":["comment fields","communication design","editorial control","journalism","moderation","online comments","user experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CBFA6537733DDDADE9F830C65667B6B2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81970782/User_Experiences_with_Editorial_Control_in_Online_Newspaper_Comment_Fields.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17512786.2017.1293490","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"westerdals oslo school of arts","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Westerdals Oslo School of Arts","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Andrea","key":"ihlebækpau","last":"Ihlebæk","name":"Ihlebæk, Karoline Andrea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Olof","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Anders Olof","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17512786.2017.1293490","issn":["14616211","17512786"],"issn_org":["17512786"],"journal":"Journalism Practice","pages":"1-20","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journalism Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014575944"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4573861e-0bb4-49d7-9ebf-defa5924e6b1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"User experiences with editorial control in online newspaper comment fields","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382298","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Hackathon-style events are increasingly used to facilitate cross-disciplinary learning and innovation in the media industries. Based on an observational study of a hackathon organized as part of the film festival Nordic Panorama (NP) we analyse the challenges in using the hackathon format to facilitate cross-disciplinary learning and innovation for filmmakers, developers and designers. We find that many participants experienced frustrations resulting from a lack of programming skills and their expectation that the hackathon should result in ‘something digital’. Additionally, ideals for authorship embedded in the working cultures of film and TV professionals impeded the team’s ability to involve all participants on an equal footing. As implications for future hackathons we suggest organizers should consider using tools for end-user development and generative toolkits to facilitate digital making and collaborative learning. We also suggest similar events should avoid including project owners if the group work is based on existing projects.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Karlsen, Joakim","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Østfold University College"],"keyword":["Design","Film","Hackathon","Hacker culture","Media work"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"you can dance your prototype if you like independent filmmakers adapting the hackathon","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82060243/digital_creativity_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384487","identifier":[{"id":"85025174315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-db219f4f-aa9c-43d5-8f71-32a3b971757e"],"keyword":["Design","Film","Hackathon","Hacker culture","Media work"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CDB8E0B8799B67FBDA3CB9040D4576DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82060243/digital_creativity_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"østfold university college","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Østfold University College","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joakim","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","name":"Karlsen, Joakim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/14626268.2017.1351992","issn":["14626268","17443806"],"issn_org":["14626268"],"issue":"3","journal":"Digital Creativity","pages":"224-239","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Digital Creativity","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025174315"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db219f4f-aa9c-43d5-8f71-32a3b971757e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘You can dance your prototype if you like’: independent filmmakers adapting the hackathon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384487","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
