{"abstract":"Innovating in the field of new media genres requires methods for producing designs that can succeed in being disseminated and used outside of design research labs. This article uses the author's experiences with the development of university courses in communication design to address the research question: How can we design courses to give students the competencies they need to work as designers of new media? Based on existing approaches from UX design and other fields, I present a model that has demonstrated its usefulness in the development of commercial products and services. The model emphasises rapid techniques for user research and ideation; genre analysis; use of pitching and storytelling as a form of prototyping; and humanist methods for evaluation and critique.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381457"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design education","Genre","Ideation","Innovation","Lifecycle model","Media design","NABC","Research through Design","User Experience Design","communication design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing communication design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81549709/designing_com_design_pub.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381457","ids":["itu-0cdea39d-e41a-46bb-9416-96ea21f65b6e"],"keyword":["NABC","communication design","design education","genre","ideation","innovation","lifecycle model","media design","research through design","user experience design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3CDC15E1DE38757EEFFB6CB36FE145E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81549709/designing_com_design_pub.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://www.journals.uio.no/index.php/TJMI/article/view/2486","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18945562"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Media Innovations","publisher":"Centre for Research on Media Innovations","status":"p","title":"Journal of Media Innovations","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0cdea39d-e41a-46bb-9416-96ea21f65b6e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing Communication Design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381457","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this ethnographic study is to explore the smartphone’s role in the contemporary international backpacking experience. This paper will examine backpackers’ perceived changes in mediated relations and personal attitudes towards phone use in co-present situations pre-trip, on-trip, and post-trip. Urry & Larsen’s theory on tourist performances as well as Paris et al.’s experiences of technology induced anxieties and tensions while traveling provide a conceptual framework for the analysis. A sample of 11 backpackers were interviewed at youth dormitories in Bali and Malaysia. Post-trip interviews were conducted primarily online through Skype. The findings suggest that there is an ideal of staying offline while traveling. Yet, backpackers report connecting daily with their smartphones and reveal a travel-time legitimacy for sharing updates and receiving attention on social media. After the trip, backpackers perceive a reduction in their own phone use and an increased tolerance for others’ phone use in their presence.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Silas, Everiin","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Ling, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383949"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanyang Technological University"],"keyword":["Smartphone Norms Backpacking Ethnography Dependency Social skills"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the smartphone s role in the contemporary backpacking experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ojs.meccsa.org.uk/index.php/netknow/article/view/491","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383949","ids":["itu-b7d2ade1-73a8-4b75-b5bd-757d2f1a4315"],"keyword":["Smartphone, Norms, Backpacking, Ethnography, Dependency, Social skills"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B322AED652AFB2EF8A3ECA2ECA2F2821"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419425/Silasetalthesmartphonesrolecorrected.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ojs.meccsa.org.uk/index.php/netknow/article/view/491","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/312043916","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Digital Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Everiin","key":"silaspau","last":"Silas","name":"Silas, Everiin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"lingpau","last":"Ling","name":"Ling, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["17559944"],"issue":"6","journal":"Networking Knowledge: Journal of the MeCCSA Postgraduate Network","pages":"40-53","publisher":"Media, Communication and Cultural Studies Association","status":"p","title":"Networking Knowledge: Journal of the MeCCSA Postgraduate Network","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7d2ade1-73a8-4b75-b5bd-757d2f1a4315"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The smartphone’s role in the contemporary backpacking experience","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383949","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates user experiences with editorial control of online comments sections in online newspapers, in light of the public backlash against online comments after the 2011 terror attacks in Norway. We analyse data from a quantitative survey (N=3470) among users of four newspaper websites, in order to understand different user groups' experiences and attitudes towards editorial control against a spectrum between liberal and interventionist positions. We find that the liberals tend to be male, participate more frequently, prefer anonymity and rate the quality of the debates higher than the interventionists. Regarding their experiences with control, liberals have more often had their comments edited or removed by moderators, and have more often not understood why this was done. They also believe that moderation has become more strict, and that their opportunities to speak their minds freely have become worse after the terror attacks.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Ihlebæk, Karoline Andrea","Larsson, Anders Olof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384098"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-13","place":"Fukuoka, jp","start":"2016-06-09","title":"The 66th Annual Conference of the International Communication Association","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Westerdals Oslo School of Arts"],"keyword":["Editorial Control","Moderation Practices","Newspaper Websites","Online comments","User experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user experiences with editorial control in online comments sections after the 000000002011 terror attacks in norway","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384098","ids":["itu-c1cea5b0-19d8-4cb1-bfe9-4622a5c361c0"],"keyword":["Editorial Control","Moderation Practices","Newspaper Websites","Online Comments","User Experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01206DAD9CDA2AA5959F7023AD93BB46"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Digital Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"westerdals oslo school of arts","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Westerdals Oslo School of Arts","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Andrea","key":"ihlebækpau","last":"Ihlebæk","name":"Ihlebæk, Karoline Andrea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Olof","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Anders Olof","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1cea5b0-19d8-4cb1-bfe9-4622a5c361c0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"User Experiences With Editorial Control in Online Comments Sections After the 2011 Terror Attacks in Norway","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384098","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This chapter presents an experiment in facilitating public contributions to an experimental system for locative literature called textopia. Discussing approaches to collaborative writing and the relationship between games and art, the paper presents the development and the testing of a game designed to foster participation in the system. The game is based on the recombination of found texts into literary compositions, integrating the act of exploring the urban environment into the act of writing, as well as into the medium that is studied. The resulting texts are read as a form of situated, poetic documentary reports on the urban textual environment. The experiment also draws attention to the importance of live events in building a literary community.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381587"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creativity","Design","Electronic literature","Pervasive games","locative media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flâneur a walkthrough locative literature as participation and play","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://muse.jhu.edu/chapter/1746709","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381587","identifier":[{"id":"85038599299","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-14d478e0-ded7-4e71-8ef2-7b0de3ad8610"],"keyword":["creativity","design","electronic literature","locative media","pervasive games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-512DD0C5199A134FD6A7555BC2F403C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://muse.jhu.edu/chapter/1746709","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Scott","key":"rettbergpedh","last":"Rettberg","name":"Rettberg, Scott","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Patricia","key":"tomaszekpedh","last":"Tomaszek","name":"Tomaszek, Patricia","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sandy","key":"baldwinpedh","last":"Baldwin","name":"Baldwin, Sandy","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781943665013"],"isbn":["9781940425993"],"pages":"151-168","place":"Morgantown","publisher":"Center for Literary Computing","series":"Computing Literature","status":"p","title":"Electronic LIterature Communications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-14d478e0-ded7-4e71-8ef2-7b0de3ad8610"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Flâneur, a Walkthrough : Locative Literature as Participation and Play","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381587","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
